From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Heinemeier Hansson <david@hey.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 14:13:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2754] arm64: dts: qcom: x1p42100-asus-zenbook-14-ux3480qa: Disable
 CoreSight

The Zenbook 14 UX3480QAB, the UX3480QA under a model number ending in
B, resets with no panic about half a second after qcom_aoss binds.
qcom_aoss provides the QDSS clock that hamoa.dtsi's CoreSight blocks
(STM, TPDM, TPDA, funnels, replicators, TMCs, CTIs and the CTCU) take
as their apb_pclk. None of them carries arm,primecell-periphid, so once
the clock exists the AMBA bus enables it and reads each block's
peripheral ID, built-in code that runs without any CoreSight driver.

On the UX3480QAB (BIOS UX3480QAB.304), booting the live initramfs and
loading its modules one at a time: with qcom_aoss blocked it never
resets, and NVMe, USB and the keyboard come up; with qcom_aoss loaded it
resets within half a second of its successful probe, whatever loads
next; with these 53 nodes disabled and qcom_aoss loaded it does not
reset. The UX3480QA (BIOS UX3480QA.303) boots with them enabled.

Disable the trace path in the tree both machines share. Nothing uses
tracing.
